-- title:
--   Principal divisors generated by A-primitive functions and diamond translates
-- statement:
--   Let $M \geq 1$, let $H$ be a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$, let $\ell$ be a prime not dividing $M$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` with $\ell$ a non-unit of $A$ (the predicate `LiesOverPrime`), so $A$ has residue map onto its residue field. Assume `HeckeDiamondInputsHAll M H`, that is: for every prime the predicate `HeckeInputsHAlong (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) M H` holds at it, and for every $d \in (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$ there exists a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of $F :=$ `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` (the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$, of `xHFunctionField M H`) satisfying `IsDiamondAutHBar M H d σ`; and fix $d \in (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$. Then the subgroup of principal divisors of $F/\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ — divisors $D$, finitely supported functions on the places $P$ of $F/\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (valuation subrings of $F$ containing $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, proper, with principal ideals), for which some $f \neq 0$ in $F$ has $D(P) = \operatorname{ord}_P(f)$ for all $P$ — is contained in the additive subgroup generated by those $D$ for which there are Laurent series $y, u$ over $A$ such that: the coefficientwise image of $y$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ lies in $F$, the coefficientwise image of $u$ equals `diamondAutHBar M H d` applied to that element of $F$, the coefficientwise reductions of $y$ and of $u$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ both lie in `xHFunctionFieldC (IsLocalRing.ResidueField A) M H` (the $q$-expansion function field for $\Gamma_H(M)$ over the residue field) and are both nonzero, and $D(P) = \operatorname{ord}_P$ of the element of $F$ determined by $y$, for every place $P$.
--
--   This is a $q$-expansion principle of generation type: every divisor class of $X_H(M)$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is represented by sums of divisors of functions that are $A$-integral with nonzero reduction at the cusp $\infty$, simultaneously for the function and for its image under the diamond automorphism $\langle d \rangle$. It is used in the construction of the reduction modulo $\ell$ of Hecke correspondences on $X_H(M)$, via [`ModularCurve.reductionQExpModL_gammaH_heckeOperatorHAlong`](thm.html#ModularCurve.reductionQExpModL_gammaH_heckeOperatorHAlong).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_principal_le_closure_divisor_laurentIntegral_diamondAutHBar.lean

